// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Tactical_Ops 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4228715576" "These are the backbone of the military presence of the Malta Group. The Tac Ops cells are trained to operate independently and are almost never aware of each others activity. Machine guns, grenades of varying kinds and other modern weaponry are their stock in trade."
// DisplayNames :
"P3591016325" "Tactical Operative"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Tactical_Ops_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3051145037" "Operation Officer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Tactical_Ops_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3404517659" "The Tac Ops Commanders are the only members of their cell to have any contact with the upper echelons of the Malta group. Secrecy and maintaining their cover identity is the primary directive for these agents."
// DisplayNames :
"P1241455952" "Tac Ops Commander"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Tactical_Ops_Engineer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1520027628" "The Engineers of the Tac Ops cells are masters of technology. They maintain and repair all the equipment used by their comrades. In addition to these responsibilities the Engineers are known to drop turrets in the field, turning every battle with their cell into a killing field."
// DisplayNames :
"P4199269174" "Operation Engineer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Sapper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2975561318" "It has not yet been fully determined how the Bio-Energy Feedback Inducer utilized by the Malta Sappers works, but it certainly does so efficiently. It is clear this weapon was designed specifically for hunting down and neutralizing super powered beings of all sorts. Heroes in combat with them should be very wary."
// DisplayNames :
"P113623609" "Sapper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Gunslinger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P792487674" "Some of the most deadly operatives in the Malta Group have been given the nickname Gunslingers. This name came into common usage not only because the agents use firearms, but because they also tend to have the same kind of cocky attitude and cowboy mentality that one associates with gunslingers in the old west."
// DisplayNames :
"P3872227952" "Gunslinger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Gunslinger_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1576689983" "Any Gunslinger might be able to take down a super powered being, especially the experienced ones. Their mastery of the deadly weaponry and technology given to them by the Malta Group is complete. They complete the tasks assigned to them, taking pleasure in violence, especially when they get the chance to take down some heroes in the process."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Gyrfalcon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2160369046" "Gyrfalcon is the Malta Group's top general and the only known member of the organization's mysterious Council of Leaders. Though Gyrfalcon has an almost legendary disdain for his operatives, when they get killed or captured, he does something about it. That, after all, is what you do."
// DisplayNames :
"P2648933782" "Gyrfalcon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Gyrfalcon_Ally 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Hercules_Titan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1919039370" "The Hercules class is the smallest Titan unit employed by Malta. It is believed that the technology used to create them came to this covert villain group sometime during or after the fall of the Soviet Union. It has not yet been determined if the Titans are simply robots, or something more. Their offensive capabilities are many and varied."
// DisplayNames :
"P2458251683" "Hercules Class Titan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Hercules_Titan_NoMerge 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Zeus_Titan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P793950004" "The middle class of Titans utilized by the Malta Group are even more deadly than their younger brothers. This stands to reason since they are two Hercules class units combined into one deadly enemy. They are equipped with the standard fragmentation, incendiary and gas missiles. In addition the Zeus units combined plasma generators are extremely potent, firing multiple blasts simultaneously."
// DisplayNames :
"P3910698076" "Zeus Class Titan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Zeus_Spawner 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Zeus_Merged_Titan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Kronos_Titan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P859541547" "The mammoth Kronos Class Titans are the pinnacle of the Titan project. Fortunately they are prohibitively expensive to manufacture. If the Malta Group can find a cost effective way of manufacturing these monsters, their terror will felt around the globe."
// DisplayNames :
"P1952089346" "Kronos Class Titan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Mission_Kronos_Titan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayClassName :
"P3957587816" "Monster"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Mine 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P466688635" "Trip Mine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2938275991" "The Engineers of the Tac Ops team has constructed this Turret.  Its defenses are surely formidable."
// DisplayNames :
"P2023029757" "Auto Turret"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Malta_Gas 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// GroupDescription :
"P1065236535" "Gas"
// DisplayNames :
"P1959652309" "Poison Gas"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
