// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Battle_Orb_Mk_1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P486841953" "Battle Orbs are equipped with a wide variety of equipment loads. Some units serve a defensive and support oriented role, while others are more about bringing additional suppressive fire and offense."
// DisplayNames :
"P2923670276" "Battle Orb Mk I"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Battle_Orb_Mk_2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3670118667" "Battle Orb Mk II"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Battle_Orb_Mk_3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1242173088" "Battle Orb Mk III"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Warworks_Drone 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P139011817" "Warworks Drones are rapid assault weapons dispatched by the Warworks Drone Carriers equipped with highly advanced plasma weapons capable of weakening even the toughest of super powered beings."
// DisplayNames :
"P793394784" "Drone"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Chemical_Burn 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P388952242" "The most advanced of the Warworks shock troopers. These towering androids carry a heavy PGMP Rifle that is capable of delivering a deadly neurotoxin payload."
// DisplayNames :
"P3443609182" "Chemical Burn"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Assault_Trooper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1943650702" "Tyrant's Imperial Defense Force troopers are the most advanced soldiers in his arsenal. The IDF Assault Troopers are equipped with an upgraded Plasma Glove and Power Armor with jump boosters, making them resistant to all types of damage."
// DisplayNames :
"P2376363524" "Assault Trooper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Ranger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2302002835" "Tyrant's Imperial Defense Force troopers are the most advanced soldiers in his arsenal. The IDF Rangers are equipped with an upgraded Plasma Glove and Power Armor, making them resistant to all types of damage."
// DisplayNames :
"P1681294533" "Ranger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Shock_Trooper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3584830775" "Tyrant's Imperial Defense Force Troopers are the most advanced soldiers in his arsenal. The IDF Shock Troopers are terrifying foes to engage. Their weaponry is far more advanced than the PPD Shock Glove, and they are decked out in nearly impenetrable power armor."
// DisplayNames :
"P1357981292" "Shock Trooper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Elite_Ranger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3001854750" "Tyrant's Imperial Defense Force troopers are the most advanced soldiers in his arsenal. The IDF Elite Rangers are terrifying foes to engage. Their weaponry is far more advanced than the PPD Shock Glove, and they are decked out in nearly impenetrable power armor."
// DisplayNames :
"P2334395702" "Elite Ranger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Heavy_Trooper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4225690044" "Tyrant's Imperial Defense Force troopers are the most advanced soldiers in his arsenal. The IDF Heavy Troopers wear heavy Power Armor with jump boosters as well as shoulder mounted rocket launchers that are capable of delivering a powerful nerve gas that can cripple enemies."
// DisplayNames :
"P2354525606" "Heavy Trooper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Commander 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P377725382" "Tyrant's Imperial Defense Force troopers are the most advanced soldiers in his arsenal. IDF Commanders lead the IDF Forces to war offering a frightening array of plasma weaponry. They have little need of bulky powered armor, their innate superior genetic structure proving to be more than a match for conventional weapons."
// DisplayNames :
"P3223493145" "Commander"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Heavy_Commander 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P955342276" "IDF Heavy Commanders can lead the Heavy Troopers into combat or occasionally supply heavy support on their own to a unit. They overcome the short range flaws of the Heavy Trooper with the addition of plasma machine guns to handle close range foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P785683335" "Heavy Commander"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Olympian_Guard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1892167528" "These soldiers are said to be the recipients of the most advanced genetic and bio-engineering Praetoria has to offer. Only Tyrant and his Praetors are more powerful than the mighty Olympian Guard."
// DisplayNames :
"P509661734" "Olympian Guard"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Mobile_Artillery 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P833407285" "IDF Mobile Artillery is an enhanced soldier with the most advance heavy artillery equipment available. Combining short, medium, and long range arms, the Mobile Artillery is a almost a WarWorks Goliath's worth of hurt in a much more dexterous and mobile package."
// DisplayNames :
"P1037359178" "Mobile Artillery"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Warworks_Mobile_Defense_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P662588807" "Armed with plasma weaponry capable of piercing through the toughest of armor, these turrets are an incredibly effective deterrent for keeping trespassers out of the Lambda sector and other vital Praetorian military outposts."
// DisplayNames :
"P3764452896" "Mobile Defense Turret"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Warworks_Reactor_Defense_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2758716191" "Armed with extensive multi-phasic sensor arrays and plasma weaponry capable of piercing through the toughest of armor, these turrets are an incredibly effective deterrent for keeping trespassers out of Lambda Sector, Keyes Island and other vital Praetorian military outposts."
// DisplayNames :
"P874746666" "Maximum Defense Turret"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Warworks_Seeker_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3118552339" "Armed with extensive multi-phasic sensor arrays and plasma weaponry capable of piercing through the toughest of armor, these turrets are used to assist in anti-Resistance operations and search-and-destroy missions."
// DisplayNames :
"P1274115058" "Seeker Turret"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_DUSTRanger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2485837114" "The Direct Urban Strike Team, or D.U.S.T., are an elite unit of the T.E.S.T. forces equipped to deal with counterinsurgency and urban combat. They are trained to deal with the Devouring Earth and other unusual threats, making them the premier force for deployment in times of dire need. They are equipped with a unique variant of standard T.E.S.T. armor and with a specialized plasma cannon that has a variety of firing modes. The Rangers are among the most elite soldiers in the PPD, able to survive deployments in harsh conditions for months at a time."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_DUSTLeader 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3345044944" "The Direct Urban Strike Team, or D.U.S.T., are an elite unit of the T.E.S.T. forces equipped to deal with counterinsurgency and urban combat. They are trained to deal with the Devouring Earth and other unusual threats, making them the premier force for deployment in times of dire need. They are equipped with a unique variant of standard T.E.S.T. armor and with a specialized plasma cannon that has a variety of firing modes. The Leaders have experience improvising with the weapon, and are infamous for poisoning their enemies with weaponized flamer fuel."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_DUSTProvost 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3022640472" "The Direct Urban Strike Team, or D.U.S.T., are an elite unit of the T.E.S.T. forces equipped to deal with counterinsurgency and urban combat. They are trained to deal with the Devouring Earth and other unusual threats, making them the premier force for deployment in times of dire need. They are equipped with a unique variant of standard T.E.S.T. armor and with a specialized plasma cannon that has a variety of firing modes. The Provosts are very well trained in the use of their weapon and are feared by all who work against Cole's will."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianDUSTIDFEndgame_Olympian_Guard_Ally 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayClassName :
"P2664220932" "Boss"

