"P882889850" "Mk-VI "Victoria""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Warworks_War_Walker 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2569777715" "War Walkers are meant to serve one purpose, to instill terror into its foes as it obliterates them with its deadly particle cannons. The mechanical behemoths represent the pinnacle of Praetorian technology."
// DisplayNames :
"P4105718507" "War Walker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Warworks_Goliath_War_Walker 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1154066920" "The dreadnaughts tend to lead invasion forces due to their incredible resilience and destructive prowess. Wherever the Goliath War Walker goes, a trail of destruction is left in its wake."
// DisplayNames :
"P4154397344" "Goliath War Walker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Warworks_Defense_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
// DisplayNames :
"P1386486994" "Defense Turret"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Warworks_Mobile_Defense_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Seer_Scryer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P818779251" "Scyers are among the elite of Mother Mayhem's Seers. They make up the rank and file combatants among the elite. They specialize in tearing their foes minds apart with their mental assault while peering into the mind of their foes to find their weakness."
// DisplayNames :
"P3655164509" "Scryer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Seer_Seeker 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1707654086" "Seekers are among the elite of Mother Mayhem's Seers. They make up the rank and file combatants among the elite. Seekers have the ability to mend others wounds with their minds as well as augment their allies with mental wards."
// DisplayNames :
"P2230423493" "Seeker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Seer_Diviner 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1493841138" "Diviners are among the elite of Mother Mayhem's Seers. They are mid-rank combatants among the elite. They specialize in crushing their foes in close range combat."
// DisplayNames :
"P3601274040" "Diviner"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Seer_Augur 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1791998782" "Augurs are the elite amongst the Seers and are masters of mind control. They are capable of crippling their enemies with powerful mental assaults then moving in for the kill."
// DisplayNames :
"P1586206284" "Augur"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Terminal_Field 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// GroupDescription :
// DisplayNames :
"P491780887" "Terminal Field"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Riptide 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4177369014" "Riptide's frightening appearance is matched only by his brutality in combat. He can discharge lethal amounts of bio-electricity on anyone who gets too close, while clusters of retractable poisonous spines discourage anyone from staying within arms reach. Despite his monstrous countenance, Riptide is an honorable man outside of combat, but start a fight with him, and all semblance of civility is tabled until victory is had."
// DisplayNames :
"P1612539309" "Riptide"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Fusion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1031169856" "Fusion is powered by an internal nuclear reactor which grants him the ability to focus massive waves of force outward. It is a hotly debated question as to why Fusion's Primal Earth double, Fusionette, is not the same gender as he."
// DisplayNames :
"P789767047" "Fusion"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Jane_Temblor 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2225505768" "Jane Temblor, aka Faultline, is the Praetorian double of hero Jim Temblor. Jane's history is similar to Jim's, despite the obvious, though there are rumors her Earth control has something to do with a possible Devouring Earth influence on her parents."
// DisplayNames :
"P1929037949" "Jane Temblor"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Duray 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P668161439" "The field commander of the late General Aarons' Threat Response Battalion, Colonel Virgil Duray is one of the most highly decorated officers from the Hamidon Wars. The TRB, nicknamed Tribe, was the only conventionally armed military force to achieve consistent victories over the Devouring Earth.<br><br>Duray has since been put in command of the latest and greatest of Praetoria's Special Forces; The Imperial Defense Force's 2nd Battalion. Composed entirely of soldiers from the TRB, the 2nd Battalion is arguably just a rename of Duray's former command with one exceptional difference. Every soldier in the battalion has been genetically reengineered by Praetor Berry."
// DisplayNames :
"P2602517941" "Colonel Duray"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Duray_Clone 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P10865947" "Clone of Colonel Duray"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianIDF_Duray_Backup_Timer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2341890537" "Backup Copy"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
