// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Trooper_Tutorial 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3672913708" "The Praetoria Police Department is charged with the unending duty of maintaining order on the streets of the City. These tireless men and women watch over Praetoria City, dedicating their lives to serving Emperor Cole...and the populace, of course."
// DisplayNames :
"P3405929432" "PPD Trooper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Suppressor_Tutorial 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2257032941" "PPD Suppressor"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Enforcer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Trooper 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Suppressor 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Monitor_Sphere 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4209977243" "The Praetoria Police Department is charged with the unending duty of maintaining order on the streets of the City. The Monitor Sphere is an invaluable piece of equipment for the officers charged with this duty."
// DisplayNames :
"P1520885849" "Monitor Sphere"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Warrant_Officer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1157181857" "Warrant Officers are promoted from the ranks of the Troopers based on their loyalty to the PPD. They are often responsible for dispatching troops into dangerous situations. They understand very clearly the risk that comes with a PPD uniform."
// DisplayNames :
"P3848404012" "PPD Warrant Officer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Justicar 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2595491573" "Justicars are promoted from the ranks of the Troopers based on their loyalty to the PPD.  They've received additional training on using their Force Gauntlet in hand to hand combat.  They can super charge it allowing a tremendous burst of force."
// DisplayNames :
"P1661729777" "PPD Justicar"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Sergeant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P15034690" "Sergeants are high ranking officers who have worked their way to the top through loyalty and diligence and have been equipped with top of the line 'non-lethal' force weaponry."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Investigator 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1274660347" "These senior officers are masters of investigation and uncovering evidence that leads to conviction after conviction. Once they are on the trail, no one is safe from their relentless pursuit. No one."
// DisplayNames :
"P2982606177" "PPD Investigator"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_Interrogator 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3514347619" "The flash of a silver trenchcoat that accompanies the arrival of a PPD Investigator is enough to send a thrill of fear down the spine of any resident of Praetoria. If an Investigator has arrived at your door then you should already be planning your full-throated confession."
// DisplayNames :
"P3423663077" "PPD Interrogator"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_TEST_Ranger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3202429529" "The final physical challenge that a member of the PPD goes through in order to be admitted into the Tactical Engagement Strike Team is speculated about in hushed whispers all over Praetoria. Those who succeed won't speak of it and those who fail don't survive the experience."
// DisplayNames :
"P3987239186" "T.E.S.T. Ranger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_TEST_Leader 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3991243719" "Tactical Engagement Strike Team Leaders are always selected from within the ranks. They are trained to take down lawbreakers hard and fast with no concern for secondary objectives like avoiding collateral damage."
// DisplayNames :
"P2077301302" "T.E.S.T. Leader"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_PPD_TEST_Provost 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3647034139" "Anything that pulls a PPD Provost out of their Monitor Sphere information nexus has to be considered a severe threat. In order to insure their safety, Provosts don the state of the art in PPD protective gear to restore order in the most extreme cases of lawbreaking."
// DisplayNames :
"P2779402064" "T.E.S.T. Provost"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Chief_Interrogator_Washington 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1131638368" "Washington is a man that only those who seek to harm the safety of Praetoria should fear. Those who do fear him make sure to avoid him at all cost, due to Washington's animal-like instincts and ruthless fighting style."
// DisplayClassName :
"P4141179286" "Interrogator"
// DisplayNames :
"P3979306182" "Chief Interrogator Washington"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Cleopatra 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1826675707" "Cleopatra is a woman who has fought every moment to get where she is today. Despite having everything she could have when she was growing up, she wanted to live the life of a fighter. She received nothing but the best training and has proved herself to not only be a high ranking member of the Loyalist, but also Praetor White's girlfriend."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2333937975" "Loyalist"
// GroupDescription :
"P1106710767" "Powers Division"
// DisplayNames :
"P2826091210" "Cleopatra"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Reese_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P12752895" "Cocky and self-centered, Reese has good reason to throw his weight around Powers Division. Of all of Marauder's Top Dogs none have risen higher or faster than him. No other Powers Division member can match Reese's strength, skill, and cunning, a point he makes abundantly clear with the broken bodies of those who would dare challenge him."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2895398443" "Top Dog"
// DisplayNames :
"P4292860590" "Reese"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Reese 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Aria 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P691728466" "As dangerous as she is beautiful, Aria is the alluring siren of the Powers Division's Top Dogs. Her mastery over illusion has allowed her to defeat rivals without lifting a finger, and her musical laughter can quickly turn deadly if you cross her."
// DisplayNames :
"P3675512154" "Aria"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Aria_NoPowers 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Stern 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1603616157" "Stern has been replacing his body with cybernetics his entire life. Born a quadriplegic, Stern's only dream was to be a hero and to help others. He was given that chance when a mysterious benefactor offered to give him the body of a true hero. He has since gained recognition amongst the Powers Division and earned a place in the Top Dogs. His steady detachment from humanity, however, has given him a reputation as a ruthless and uncaring adversary."
// DisplayNames :
"P2765302573" "Stern"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Riptide 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Zane 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3949105709" "Zane and Reese have had a rivalry since they both joined Powers Division. Constantly chasing Reese for the top spot, Zane has remained adamant that he can and will defeat Reese, a claim he has yet to prove. Despite this, Zane is tougher than any other Top Dog, and has earned the respect of Powers Division as a strong and honorable ally."
// DisplayNames :
"P172442163" "Zane"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Warrant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2122913280" "Determined and dependable, Warrant rose from the ranks of the PPD and into the Powers Division. His custom armor is not only symbolic of his dedication to Praetoria, but it also packs quite a bit more punch than the gear issued to the police."
// DisplayNames :
"P529620251" "Warrant"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Welks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P953266527" "One of the few female officers on the force, Sheila Welks does a job that few women in Praetoria would want to. It's hard work, but Welks is proud to be doing it. She was recently promoted to Warrant Officer after rescuing a fellow officer from Destroyers and still managing to bring them into custody, albeit with a few broken bones."
// DisplayClassName :
"P8909797" "PPD Officer"
// DisplayNames :
"P1882927766" "Warrant Officer Welks"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Kang 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4103853195" "Interrogator Kang is one of the veteran agents of the Ministry of Intelligence. He is known to be one of the best case workers in the city because he was working the job before Seers came along."
// DisplayNames :
"P1043589078" "Interrogator Kang"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Jim_Donner 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P312425218" "Jim Donner is known for being the former partner of James Noble. The two together were one of the best officers in all of Praetoria. After James died serving overseas, Jim looked after his wife and child. Jim eventually married Jennifer and has since sworn to serve the people of Praetoria in the name of James Noble."
// DisplayNames :
"P2921006360" "Jim Donner"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Olympian_Experiment 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3310008501" "Neuron's genetic engineering experiments at recreating Marcus Cole have reached a viable state, though its power pales in comparison to the Emperor."
// GroupDescription :
"P1546804066" "Experiment"
// DisplayNames :
"P3761926282" "Cole's Clone"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Olympian_Experiment_Vat 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Lambda_Cole_Clone 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayClassName :
"P766296796" "Clone"
// DisplayNames :
"P3918764795" "Developing Clone"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_TPN_Monitor_Sphere 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P967903673" "These Monitor Spheres have been 'acquired' by H.D. They are used for his own personal interests, and are permanently linked to the TPN Campus broadcasting center, allowing H.D. to bring the news of the day live and uncensored directly into the living rooms of Praetoria's citizenry."
// GroupDescription :
"P99894250" "H.D."
// DisplayNames :
"P1610591457" "TPN Camera"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PraetorianPolice_Reese_Endgame 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1263304776" "Reese was once one of the 'Top Dogs' within the Powers Division. He went through a falling out with several members of the organization and was thought dead. However, he survived due to the kindness of some strangers within the tunnels of Praetoria. He has been fighting in the wilds of Praetoria ever since, seeking to prove to everyone in Praetoria that he is truly the 'Top Dog', the most powerful super-powered being in Praetoria."

