// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Sprocket 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1449789770" "These pint-sized Clockwork are a lot tougher than their counterparts in Paragon City. Powered by the incredible mind of the telekinetic Clockwork King, the Sprockets can deal out massive bolts of psychic energy."
// DisplayNames :
"P764994010" "Sprocket"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Summoned_Sprocket 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Summoned_Gears 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2121271238" "Gears emerge from the remnants of destroyed Clockwork Princes. Though tiny, they can still pack quite a punch."
// DisplayNames :
"P2876701861" "Gear"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Oscillator 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P344838345" "The airborne Clockwork Oscillators are a deadly threat to flying and grounded heroes alike. Like the Sprockets, these high-flying mechanical men attack using bolts of psychic energy. They are highly resistant to any psychological attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P1788816493" "Prototype Oscillator"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Lieutenant_Cannon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1904886217" "The Knights make up the bulk of the leadership class within the twisted court of the Clockwork King. Cannon Knights possess powerful, long range psychic attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P1244255544" "Cannon Knight"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Lieutenant_Lance 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P506171343" "Knight Lance"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Boss_Cannon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2815766796" "Like any monarch, the Clockwork King has his own court, although in his case it's composed of mechanical nobles called Dukes. These oversized robots are dangerous foes, possessing powerful long range mental attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P949253819" "Cannon Duke"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Boss_Lance 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2418432730" "Like any monarch, the Clockwork King has his own court, although in his case it's composed of mechanical nobles called Dukes. The Dukes Lancers are dangerous foes, possessing the ability to dominate foes with their mental powers."
// DisplayNames :
"P2144858934" "Duke Lancer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Boss_Assembler 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3471452334" "Like any monarch, the Clockwork King has his own court, although in his case it's composed of mechanical nobles called Dukes. The Assembler Dukes can summon more Clockwork minions to their side during battle."
// DisplayNames :
"P177481604" "Assembler Duke"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Prince_Cannon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1816769614" "The heirs apparent to the Clockwork King's throne, the Princes represent the pinnacle of the mad genius' creations. Although Cannon Princes sometimes seem almost human because of their advanced robotic brains, they're still highly resistant to mental attacks and can deal out massive psychic blasts."
// DisplayNames :
"P12427093" "Cannon Prince"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Prince_Lance 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1550117236" "The heirs apparent to the Clockwork King's throne, the Princes represent the pinnacle of the mad genius' creations. Although Lance Princes sometimes seem almost human because of their advanced robotic brains, they possess the decidedly inhuman ability to dominate their foes with their will.."
// DisplayNames :
"P3663930191" "Lance Prince"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Prince_Assembler 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3407821317" "The heirs apparent to the Clockwork King's throne, the Princes represent the pinnacle of the mad genius' creations.  Assembler Princes' powerful psychic attacks can painfully tear at the minds of even the most disciplined heroes. But it's their ability to rapidly produce more Clockwork soldiers that makes them truly insidious."
// DisplayNames :
"P1141892619" "Assembler Prince"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Lord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P915921308" "These elite soldiers are the personal guard and right hand of the Clockwork King. You can be sure that they will use all their psychic abilities to ensure his safety."
// DisplayNames :
"P3839560369" "Lord"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Clockwork_King 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P260320713" "You were always told that the Clockwork King was a remarkably gifted psychic who could accomplish great things if he were not crippled by his insanity. Here is the proof: the Clockwork King of dimension Epsilon Tau 27-2. This King seems far more in touch with his power than his counterpart in Paragon City. He won't be easy to beat!"
// DisplayNames :
"P2758452314" "Clockwork King"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Babbage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P914675884" "In Paragon City, Babbage is a force to be reckoned with. In dimension Epsilon Tau 27-2, it's a far, far greater threat. Babbage's blasts of psychic energy can make seasoned fighters quail before it. It's best not to approach without a couple of teammates."
// DisplayClassName :
// DisplayNames :
"P2717693396" "Babbage"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - PsychicClockwork_Clockwork_King_RCTF 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P103527577" "It's been known that the Clockwork King was one of the most powerful psychics on earth, but it took a direct threat to Penelope Yin, his self-adopted "Clockwork Princess" to make him unleash a portion of his immense psychic power. Unfortunately, the strain appears to have driven him even further into insanity."

